Expected elements: present

Presence holds. Exit is `/aztec-testnet`, the `Data` row carries `Real Aztec testnet data` plus 17 lines of capture prose, all three panes explain themselves, `Supply sources` is present, and no fixture content or invented source appears. `effectsMismatched: 0` is in the DOM — I extracted the exported body and the raw JSON below the cut is 46 lines ending `instructionsExecuted: 345, effectsMatched: 23, effectsMismatched: 0`. It is in a real scroll region, so I file placement, not absence.

Nothing layout-shaped moved this round. The one change — `Supply sources` re-fixed to body-less (border #c8c8c8, interior #ffffff, box still x13-119 / y287-309) — altered no geometry, so I re-file the outdent on narrower ground: the mechanism is `.panenote`'s own 8px padding nested inside `.srcnone`'s, which indents the Code pane's prose to 16px while the header label, the button and every other pane's prose sit at 8px. The paragraphs are the outlier, not the button.

New this round, and it answers the band-to-row question in layout terms: as a band the provenance cost ~190px of full width; as a row it costs 377px (y204-581) of a 383px-wide column — 38.5% of the pane that is the only one overflowing. The trade halved the width and doubled the height.

Also new: the ~577px cap is `--bt-measure-prose:68ch` on `.panenote`, so Code's 911px body can never use 334px of itself.

Fixes: widen Transaction by ~200px; drop one of the two nested paddings.

Rating: 5/10

